docs {
  # Stripe Webhooks
  
  Receive webhook events from Stripe.
  
  ## Endpoint
  POST /api/webhooks/stripe
  
  ## Authentication
  Stripe signature verification (not Bearer token)
  
  ## Description
  Webhook endpoint for receiving real-time events from Stripe about subscription 
  status changes and payment events.
  
  ## Events Handled
  - `checkout.session.completed` - Payment successful, subscription created
  - `customer.subscription.updated` - Subscription details changed
  - `customer.subscription.deleted` - Subscription cancelled/expired
  - `invoice.payment_succeeded` - Recurring payment successful
  - `invoice.payment_failed` - Recurring payment failed
  
  ## Security
  - Uses Stripe webhook signature verification
  - Verifies request authenticity with webhook secret
  - Rejects requests without valid signature
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**:
    - `{ "message": "webhookSecretNotConfigured" }` - Webhook secret not set in env
    - `{ "message": "invalidSignature" }` - Invalid Stripe signature
  
  ## Business Logic
  - Automatically updates subscription status in database
  - Updates isPro status based on subscription state
  - Handles subscription lifecycle events
  - Manages payment success/failure
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Auto-update Pro membership status
  - Track subscription changes
  - Handle payment failures
  - Manage subscription cancellations
  
  ## Notes
  - This endpoint is called by Stripe only, not by clients
  - Requires webhook secret configured in Stripe dashboard
  - Must be publicly accessible (no Bearer auth)
}
